= Choosing our enemies

In our media and campaign materials, who should we consider as our main opponents?

[? if enemies != 0 : Previously, we had considered the [+ enemies +] as our prior enemies. Is a change of direction necessary? ?]

- @anti_dem: The anti-democratic parties of the far right and left - the <span style="color: #700000;">**SED**</span> and <span style="color: #c26f2b;">**NPD**</span>.
- @cdu: The <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> and <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span>
- @bourgeois: The bourgeois parties - the <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span>, <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> and <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span>.
- @SED: The <span style="color: #700000;">**SED**</span> alone.
- @npd: The <span style="color: #c26f2b;">**NPD**</span> alone.
- @easy_discard

@anti_dem
on-arrival: enemies = "anti-democratic parties"; democratic_socialist_strength += 5; pragmatist_strength += 5; new_left_dissent += 5; workers_spd += 0.3; white_collar_workers_spd += 0.3; workers_npd -= 0.5; white_collar_workers_npd -= 0.5;

Attacking the far right and left is popular among all but the <span style="color: #94195b;">left wing</span> of our party, who would prefer to be fighting the bourgeois parties.

@cdu
on-arrival: enemies = "CDU"; democratic_socialist_strength += 5; new_left_strength += 5; pragmatist_dissent += 5; workers_cdu -= 0.8; white_collar_workers_cdu -= 0.8; cdu_relation -= 5;

Attacking our main rival is popular among all but the <span style="color: #de6a70;">pragmatist wing</span> of our party. This may make <span style="color: #C00000;">Grand</span> <span style="color: #000000;">Coalitions</span> harder to form.

@bourgeois
on-arrival: enemies = "bourgeois parties"; new_left_strength += 8; new_left_dissent -= 5; fdp_relation -= 5; cdu_relation -= 5; pragmatist_dissent += 8; workers_cdu -= 0.5; workers_fdp -= 0.5; white_collar_workers_cdu -= 0.5; white_collar_workers_fdp -= 0.5; coalition_dissent += 1

Our anti-bourgeois rhetoric is popular among the left, but may make it harder to build the coalitions that are necessary for government in the future.

@SED
on-arrival: enemies = "SED"; pragmatist_strength += 5; new_left_dissent += 8; pragmatist_dissent -= 5; fdp_relation += 5; cdu_relation += 5; workers_spd += 0.3; white_collar_workers_spd += 0.3;

Attacking <span style="color: #700000;">**SED**</span> and the East German regime is popular among the <span style="color: #de6a70;">pragmatist wing</span>.

@npd
on-arrival: enemies = "NPD"; workers_npd -= 0.8; white_collar_workers_npd -= 0.8;

[? if nsdap_r < 5 : The <span style="color: #c26f2b;">**NPD**</span> is a tiny party right now, with more bark than bite. Many in our party are questioning our choices. ?][? if nsdap_r >= 5 : The rise of the <span style="color: #c26f2b;">**NPD**</span> is very worrying. Everyone in the party likes attacking Nazis. ?]
